Scope of this licence:

This MIT licence covers the *software* portion of the deepJFET repository:
all Python scripts under tools/, blocks/, model/, simulator/, transient/,
and optimization/; all build and reproducibility tooling under paper/
(build.py, regen_data.py, reproducibility/); and the LTspice testbench
generators and corner-sweep .cir files under analysis/sweeps/.

Other parts of the repository are licensed separately:

  - The manuscript text and figures under paper/ (Main.tex, Appendices.tex,
    AppendixB.tex, AppendixC.tex, supplementary/*.tex, Images/*, bib.bib,
    bib2.bib) and the auto-generated data tables under paper/data/* are
    released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
    licence (CC-BY-4.0). See paper/LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0 for the licence text
    and https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ for the full deed.

  - The Intel 4004 architecture, the MCS-4 assembly mnemonics, and any
    waveforms or images derived from Intel-published material remain the
    intellectual property of their original owners; their inclusion here is
    for the purpose of architectural commentary and reproducibility.

Not included in this repository (and therefore NOT covered by either
licence):

  - Any proprietary SiC JFET LTspice device model or model parameter card
    that is owned by a third party. The Cree/Wolfspeed-style NJF parameters
    referenced in cpus/4004/config.py are included only to the extent that
    they appeared in the public MEng report from which this work descends;
    redistribution of any third-party-owned model card remains subject to
    the original owner's terms. Users wishing to reproduce the full
    transistor-level simulations must supply their own compatible SiC
    JFET model or obtain permission from the relevant model owner.

  - Any confidential netlist, schematic, or simulation result that the
    authors or Durham University have not explicitly chosen to publish.
